<title>UK: BP Iraqi oil contract reduced to 10,000 bpd.</title>
<headline>BP Iraqi oil contract reduced to 10,000 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc's contract to buy Iraqi crude under the U.N's oil-for-food exchange has been reduced from 20,000 barrels per day (bpd) to 10,000 bpd, trading sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BP's contract with Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation (SOMO) is now for 10,000 bpd over a six month period. Previously it was 20,000 bpd over three months, the same volume of crude over a shorter period.</p>
<p>Iraq, close to the $2 billion ceiling over six months allowed under the U.N. plan, has been obliged to cut volumes in some contracts to stay below the limit.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
